{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "P41948", "secondaryAccessions": ["D6W140"], "uniProtkbId": "MEP2_YEAST", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1995-11-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-09-02", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1995-11-01", "entryVersion": 172, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Saccharomyces cerevisiae (strain ATCC 204508 / S288c)", "commonName": "Baker's yeast", "taxonId": 559292, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Fungi", "Dikarya", "Ascomycota", "Saccharomycotina", "Saccharomycetes", "Saccharomycetales", "Saccharomycetaceae", "Saccharomyces"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9234685"}], "value": "Ammonium transporter MEP2"}}}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9234685"}], "value": "MEP2"}, "synonyms": [{"value": "AMT2"}], "orderedLocusNames": [{"value": "YNL142W"}], "orfNames": [{"value": "N1207"}, {"value": "N1820"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11069679"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11486013"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16477434"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18434596"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "24476960"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27088325"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "32069286"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9234685"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9482721"}], "value": "Transporter for ammonium (both charged and uncharged NH3 and NH4) to use as a nitrogen source (PubMed:11069679, PubMed:11486013, PubMed:16477434, PubMed:18434596, PubMed:24476960, PubMed:27088325, PubMed:9234685, PubMed:9482721). The affinity of MEP2 is about twenty times higher than that of MEP1 (PubMed:9482721). MEP3 has the lowest affinity (PubMed:9482721). Under ammonium limitation acts as an ammonium sensor, generating a signal that leads to pseudohyphal (filamentous) growth (PubMed:11069679, PubMed:16477434, PubMed:18434596, PubMed:32069286, PubMed:9482721)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES", "kineticParameters": {"maximumVelocities": [{"velocity": 18.8, "unit": "nmol/min/mg", "enzyme": "enzyme for methylammonium transport", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16477434"}]}], "michaelisConstants": [{"constant": 0.34, "unit": "mM", "substrate": "methylammonium transport", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16477434"}]}]}}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11069679"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16477434"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18434596"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "24476960"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27088325"}], "value": "Cell membrane", "id": "SL-0039"}, "topology": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27088325"}], "value": "Multi-pass membrane protein", "id": "SL-9909"}}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "32069286"}], "value": "Within the cytoplasmic CTD, an enhancer domain, limited to residues 428-441, up-regulates substrate translocation via the MEP2 hydrophobic core, while an autoinhibitory domain, comprised within the 450-485 region and including the NPR1-target serine Ser-457, counteracts the action of the enhancer domain (PubMed:32069286). In between, a linker domain, limited to residues 442-449, appears required for optimal activity when the kinase is present but dispensable when the kinase integrity is altered (PubMed:32069286)"}], "commentType": "DOMAIN"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "24476960"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27088325"}], "value": "Phosphorylated at Ser-457 by the TORC1 effector kinase NPR1 under nitrogen-limiting conditions which causes a conformational change in the C-terminal region (CTR) to form an open active conformation (PubMed:24476960, PubMed:27088325). Supplementation of nitrogen source leads to inactivation and instant Ser-457 dephosphorylation via plasma membrane PSR1 and PSR2 redundant phosphatases (PubMed:24476960)"}], "commentType": "PTM"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11069679"}], "value": "The residue Asn-4 of the protein's N-terminal tail is the only site that is glycosylated"}], "commentType": "PTM"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9482721"}], "value": "Impairs filamentation induction"}], "commentType": "DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the ammonia transporter channel (TC 1.A.11.2) family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 499, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Ammonium transporter MEP2", "featureId": "PRO_0000139755"}, {"type": "Topological domain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 31, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Extracellular", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11069679"}]}, {"type": "Transmembrane", "location": {"start": {"value": 32, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 52, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Helical; Name=1", 